# The Prettier gate is scoped to posts/ — the only directory whose bytes are
# published to the Jekyll Pages site. Everything else in this repo is authored
# to other conventions and is intentionally NOT formatted by this gate: the
# payload under plugins/ (markdown an agent executes at runtime), tests/,
# tools/, docs/, .claude/ specs and bindings, social/ drafts, and the three
# maintainer CLAUDE.md files. Whole-repo formatting is a separate effort and is
# not implied by this file.
#
# The rule: ignore everything, then unignore posts/. The npm scripts and CI run
# a bare `prettier .` from the repo root, which is where this file applies.
# (`/*` already covers node_modules/, so no separate entry.)
#
# Do NOT invert this into a list of directories to skip. An exclusion list goes
# stale the moment a directory is added, which is the enumerable-assertion trap
# CLAUDE.md documents; ignore-everything-then-unignore fails closed instead.
/*
!/posts/
